# Extraction stub — arXiv:1611.04542

This is a stub placeholder for a full Nougat OCR/MMD extraction of the
source paper. The QC-100 replication used `pdftotext -layout` (see
`work/paper.txt`) as its extraction path, not Nougat, because the
paper is a short, LaTeX-source-clean arXiv preprint whose equations
and inline math were sufficiently well-preserved by pdftotext for the
targeted quantitative reproduction (Grover k_opt, C_l1, C_r).

## What lives on-disk that plays the "extracted text" role
- `work/paper.pdf` — original arXiv PDF (fetched via curl from
  `https://arxiv.org/pdf/1611.04542`).
- `work/paper.txt` — pdftotext -layout output (this is the working
  text corpus that was consulted during claim extraction).

## If a proper Nougat extraction is later required
- Recommended: run Nougat 0.1.x against `work/paper.pdf` on the uicgpu
  A100 batch (per Rick's 2026-06-23 rule: small-batch OCR → uicgpu;
  large-batch → Polaris PBS). This paper is a single 6-page arXiv PDF,
  so uicgpu is the right target.
- Output would live at this same path (`extraction/nougat.mmd`) and
  would replace this stub verbatim.
- No re-run of the Qiskit simulation would be required; the claim-set
  (C1–C3) is stable across extraction methods.

